      "side": 1,
      "message": "`AtomicRef` is around 48 bytes whereas std::string is around 32 bytes. The biggest portion is `std::mutex`.\n\nOriginally I prefer not returning `std::string` copy in `GetLabel` because most of Graphite\u0027s labels are quite long and don\u0027t use short string optimizations. Thus every `GetLabel` call would copy the string and allocate a new heap memory. So my 1st approach makes the `ObjectLabel` immutable. `ObjectBase::SetLabel` create a new `ObjectLabel` and `ObjectBase::GetLabel` returns a ref instead.\n\nHowever, after auditing the code, it looks like `GetLabel` is called quite rarely. Only when error happens, or when backends need to set the labels (disabled by default). So maybe copying strings is acceptable?",
      "parentUuid": "0d655d8c_fb736909",
